{"graph_chars": "A demand curve holds other things equal: ceteris paribus, Latin for other things being equal. If something other than this good's price changes, the whole curve shifts. Income: for a normal good, higher income shifts demand right. Cars, Europe vacations, jewelry. For an inferior good, higher income shifts demand left. Generic groceries, used cars, renting rather than owning. Tastes: from nineteen eighty to twenty twenty-one, Americans went from forty-seven pounds of chicken a year to ninety-seven, and beef fell from seventy-six to fifty-nine. Chicken demand right, beef left. Population: more elderly means more nursing homes and hearing aids. Substitutes: a cheaper tablet cuts demand for laptops. Complements: more expensive golf clubs cut demand for golf balls. Expectations: a coming hurricane, people stock batteries today. A change in this good's own price is not on that list. Own price is a movement along the curve.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0661], [0.0661, 0.1322], [0.1322, 0.1984], [0.1984, 0.2645], [0.2645, 0.3306], [0.3306, 0.3967], [0.3967, 0.4628], [0.4628, 0.5289], [0.5289, 0.5951], [0.5951, 0.6612], [0.6612, 0.7273], [0.7273, 0.7934], [0.7934, 0.8595], [0.8595, 0.9257], [0.9257, 0.9918], [0.9918, 1.0579], [1.0579, 1.124], [1.124, 1.1901], [1.1901, 1.2562], [1.2562, 1.3224], [1.3224, 1.3885], [1.3885, 1.4546], [1.4546, 1.5207], [1.5207, 1.5868], [1.5868, 1.653], [1.653, 1.7191], [1.7191, 1.7852], [1.7852, 1.8513], [1.8513, 1.9174], [1.9174, 1.9835], [1.9835, 2.0497], [2.0497, 2.1158], [2.1158, 2.1819], [2.1819, 2.248], [2.248, 2.3141], [2.3141, 2.3803], [2.3803, 2.4464], [2.4464, 2.5125], [2.5125, 2.5786], [2.5786, 2.6447], [2.6447, 2.7108], [2.7108, 2.777], [2.777, 2.8431], [2.8431, 2.9092], [2.9092, 2.9753], [2.9753, 3.0414], [3.0414, 3.1076], [3.1076, 3.1737], [3.1737, 3.2398], [3.2398, 3.3059], [3.3059, 3.372], [3.372, 3.4382], [3.4382, 3.5043], [3.5043, 3.5704], [3.5704, 3.6365], [3.6365, 3.7026], [3.7026, 3.7687], [3.7687, 3.8349], [3.